war|armed-conflict|NOUN|armed conflict|Organized fighting using weapons between countries or opposing groups.|chiến tranh|The museum records how the war changed daily life in the town.|Bảo tàng ghi lại cách cuộc chiến tranh làm thay đổi đời sống hằng ngày trong thị trấn.|Countable for a particular conflict, uncountable for warfare generally; at war with, declare war on. No verb is proposed here.|0
appreciate|value-or-feel-grateful|VERB|value something|To recognize the value of something or feel grateful for it.|trân trọng; biết ơn|I appreciate the patience you showed during my first week at work.|Tôi trân trọng sự kiên nhẫn mà bạn đã dành cho tôi trong tuần làm việc đầu tiên.|Transitive: appreciate something or doing something; not appreciate to do. Appreciate someone means value them, not simply thank them.|0
appreciate|understand-importance|VERB|understand a situation fully|To understand a situation and recognize why it matters.|hiểu rõ và nhận thức được tầm quan trọng|After visiting the workshop, we appreciated how much skill the repairs required.|Sau khi đến xưởng, chúng tôi hiểu rõ việc sửa chữa đòi hỏi kỹ năng đến mức nào.|Appreciate a difficulty, appreciate that, appreciate how. This understanding sense need not express gratitude.|1
gallon|volume-unit|NOUN|unit of volume|A unit used to measure volume, especially the amount of a liquid.|ga-lông, đơn vị đo thể tích|The label states that the container holds one US gallon of water.|Nhãn ghi rằng bình chứa được một ga-lông Mỹ nước.|Countable: a gallon of water, two gallons. US and imperial gallons differ in size; specify the system when precision matters.|0
injure|cause-physical-harm|VERB|cause bodily harm|To cause physical damage to a person's or animal's body.|làm bị thương|The cyclist injured her shoulder when she fell on the gravel path.|Người đi xe đạp bị thương ở vai khi ngã trên lối đi rải sỏi.|Transitive: injure someone or a body part; injure yourself. Injured is the regular past form.|0
painting|painted-picture|NOUN|picture made with paint|A picture created by applying paint to a surface.|bức tranh vẽ bằng màu|The gallery displayed a painting of the harbour at dawn.|Phòng trưng bày giới thiệu một bức tranh vẽ bến cảng lúc bình minh.|Countable: a painting, several paintings; a painting of a place.|0
painting|artistic-activity|NOUN|making pictures with paint|The activity of creating pictures using paint.|việc vẽ tranh bằng màu|Painting helps Minh relax after a busy day at the office.|Việc vẽ tranh giúp Minh thư giãn sau một ngày bận rộn ở văn phòng.|Uncountable activity noun; take up painting. Not the same as an individual painting.|1
painting|coating-surfaces|NOUN|covering a surface with paint|The work of putting paint on a surface to colour or protect it.|việc sơn|The painting of the wooden fence took longer than we expected.|Việc sơn hàng rào gỗ mất nhiều thời gian hơn chúng tôi dự tính.|Uncountable activity; the painting of a wall. This decorating sense differs from making artwork.|2
